{# TASK-040: tiny 30-day pass-rate sparkline next to each Domain Health row.
   Pure inline SVG with `currentColor` so it inherits the surrounding
   text-success / text-warning / text-error tint set by the row's pass-rate
   class — no JS, no chart library.

   `points` is a list of pass-rates (0-100, oldest → newest) where a bucket that
   observed no mail at all is `null`, NOT 0. The three renderings:

     - a run of two or more consecutive measured buckets → one polyline;
     - a run of exactly one → a dot at that bucket's own x/y (it is a real
       measurement, so it must not vanish, and it must not slide to the middle
       of the box either — that would misplace it in time);
     - nothing measured anywhere → an "—" placeholder, so layout stays stable.

   Nulls BREAK the line rather than bridging it. Bridging would draw straight
   through days we never measured, which invents data; collapsing the whole
   series to "—" the moment one bucket is empty would discard the days we did
   measure. Two segments either side of a gap is the only honest option.

   The empty-series "—" is the same placeholder `pass_rate_value()` in
   `components/_severity_glyph.html.twig` renders for a null pass rate, so the
   trend line and the figure beside it always tell the same story. Before the
   buckets were nullable this promise could not be kept: `GetDomainPassRateTrend`
   coalesced empty buckets to 0.0, ten of which cleared the "two or more points"
   gate and drew a flat line along the floor — "everything failed for 30 days" —
   next to an honest "Waiting for first report". Pair this with
   `pass_rate_stat(...)`, never with a hard-coded "0.0%". #}
{% props points = [], width = 80, height = 20 %}

{% set count = points|length %}
{% set padding = 1 %}
{% set drawWidth = width - (padding * 2) %}
{% set drawHeight = height - (padding * 2) %}
{% set stepX = count > 1 ? drawWidth / (count - 1) : 0 %}

{# Split the series into runs of consecutive measured buckets. Y is inverted —
   pass_rate=100 → top of the box (y=padding), pass_rate=0 → bottom. A lone
   measured bucket in a single-bucket series is centred, which is where the eye
   expects it when there is no time axis to place it against. #}
{% set segments = [] %}
{% set run = [] %}
{% for value in points %}
    {% if value is null %}
        {% if run is not empty %}
            {% set segments = segments|merge([run]) %}
            {% set run = [] %}
        {% endif %}
    {% else %}
        {% set clamped = value < 0 ? 0 : (value > 100 ? 100 : value) %}
        {% set x = count > 1 ? padding + (loop.index0 * stepX) : width / 2 %}
        {% set y = padding + drawHeight - ((clamped / 100) * drawHeight) %}
        {% set run = run|merge([{
            x: x|number_format(2, '.', ''),
            y: y|number_format(2, '.', ''),
        }]) %}
    {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if run is not empty %}
    {% set segments = segments|merge([run]) %}
{% endif %}

{% if segments is empty %}
    <span class="inline-block align-middle text-base-content/30" style="width: {{ width }}px;" aria-hidden="true">—</span>
{% else %}
    <svg viewBox="0 0 {{ width }} {{ height }}" width="{{ width }}" height="{{ height }}"
         class="inline-block align-middle" aria-hidden="true" role="img">
        {% for segment in segments %}
            {% if segment|length >= 2 %}
                <polyline points="{{ segment|map(p => p.x ~ ',' ~ p.y)|join(' ') }}"
                          fill="none"
                          stroke="currentColor"
                          stroke-width="1.5"
                          stroke-linecap="round"
                          stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            {% else %}
                <circle cx="{{ segment[0].x }}" cy="{{ segment[0].y }}" r="1.5" fill="currentColor"/>
            {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
    </svg>
{% endif %}
